abstract: >-
  Counted trials of three experiments on CHPC notchpeak comparing a headless Claude Code baseline (2.1.295) with CLIO
  (clio-agent 0.9.5b5.post2, iowarp-core 2.2.1, factorio-flat 0.5.0 blueprint) driving the same Claude Code binary, both
  with model claude-fable-5-1, on frozen Morphorm topology-optimization workflows: E1 uninterrupted (Example 8),
  E2 interrupted recovery across two fresh sessions (Example 16) and E3 distributed context (Example 8 with sources spread
  over GitHub, Globus and a POSIX archive). Five counted trials per arm per experiment; all 30 accepted by the
  researcher-only scorer. Includes the automation, frozen task packets, per-trial records, scores, telemetry tables,
  analysis scripts, figures, methods notes and a run guide.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - Claude Code
  - CLIO
  - high-performance computing
  - topology optimization
  - Morphorm
  - Slurm
  - reproducibility
